BaseSettler_transitionIfTerminal
├── when participantCount is zero
│   └── it should return early and leave orderStatus unchanged (Pashov A1 early-return)
├── when participantCount is non-zero AND finalisedCount plus refundedCount is less than participantCount
│   └── it should return without transition
├── when all fillers are accounted for AND totalDstCstEscrowed is non-zero
│   └── it should return without transition so escrow settles before the terminal flip
├── when finalisedCount is greater than zero AND hookPhase0Done is false
│   └── it should NOT transition to Settled (hook-completion gate)
├── when finalisedCount is greater than zero AND hookPhase0Done is true AND totalDstCstEscrowed is zero
│   └── it should set orderStatus to Settled and emit OrderFinalised with status Settled
├── when refundedCount equals participantCount AND finalisedCount is zero
│   └── it should set orderStatus to Refunded and emit OrderFinalised with status Refunded
└── when the concrete is a single-participant Exact settler subclass
    └── it should treat participantCount of 1 finalisedCount of 1 and totalDstCstEscrowed of 0 as terminal (Exact special case)
